Z||000000||Standard||12-16-1999||03:03 PM||||I'm looking at an 86.5 GT 5sp that this guy is selling, he says it grinds a little going into 3rd gear.  Clutch was replaced in '98, says it just needs some adjusting.  Just wondering if it could be anything more than that.. any ideas?  Also has a leaky front manifold, which i know means it's cracked. TIA!<BR>Mike||||reg||5
Z||000001||william_thorniii||12-16-1999||07:25 PM||||This is obvious, but I have heard of it before... make sure the transmission has fluid.  That probably isn't the case though since it only grinds in third.  Unfortunately if I had to wage a guess, it would be on the synchros.  <P>Good Luck,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
Z||000002||Ed||12-16-1999||08:42 PM||||Clutch is hydraulic, doesn't have an adjustment feature: that makes me suspicious.<P>The transmission shift cable is adjustable and is very easy to do. It could be done to check before you buy. I did mine (87 GT) in about a half hour. <P>Wait! Didn't the 86.5 had a four speed?! What's up?   ||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||12-16-1999||10:22 PM||||The transsmissions available for the v-6 in '86 were 4-speed(common) and the 5-speed(quite rare) introduced later in the year.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||12-17-1999||01:22 AM||||Yes, it's a 5 speed GT Fastback! one of 2,000 made!<P>I was thinking it <B>might</B> be the syncros, but I really hope not.  I'm guessing he meant adjust the shift cables.  He posted it on the fiero mailing list, so I'm guessing he knows it's a hydraulic system.||||reg||1
